From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 20:06:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] diagnostics for the same-tick teleport refusal (D-40)

A plugin that calls Entity#teleport twice in one tick gets true then false, and
the second teleport silently does not happen. Paper performs both. Four
mechanism hypotheses have been written for this and all four were killed by
measurement rather than by argument - chunk loading, isValid(), hasNullCallback,
chunk readiness - each time by printing one more value instead of reasoning
harder. The one predicate nobody could read is hasNullCallback(), which has no
Bukkit API, so every hypothesis guessed which of canTeleportAsync()'s four
conjuncts was false from outside.

This prints them. Two hooks, both output-only:

  Entity#teleportAsync, at the refusal the platform has already decided - the
  four predicates individually, plus removal reason, callback class, ownership,
  both chunk states and the vehicle graph.

  Entity#setLevelCallback - NULL <-> set transitions only, which is the other
  half: when the entity actually leaves and rejoins the level lookup.

Off by default, prints only on a refusal or a transition, never per tick, and
returns void so it cannot influence the decision even by accident. Nothing about
lifecycle, scheduling, return values or teleport results changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
index f929dff28331882ea18b1daa99e180b9dd3795a2..6498932d3bf6efa5df43665679d1d351bbe67cef 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
@@ -4558,6 +4558,13 @@ public abstract class Entity
         }
 
         if (!this.canTeleportAsync()) {
+            // Lecithin - D-40 diagnostics: this return is the silent second teleport. Print which of
+            // canTeleportAsync()'s four predicates said no, rather than guessing from outside again.
+            // Off by default; cannot affect the refusal, which has already been decided.
+            if (fun.bm.lecithin.config.modules.CompatConfig.teleportRefusalDiagnostics) {
+                fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinTeleportRefusalDiagnostics.reportRefusal(this, destination, pos);
+            }
+            // Lecithin end
             return false;
         }
         this.getBukkitEntity(); // force bukkit entity to be created before TPing
@@ -6418,6 +6425,13 @@ public abstract class Entity
 
     @Override
     public void setLevelCallback(final EntityInLevelCallback levelCallback) {
+        // Lecithin - D-40 diagnostics: record when the entity leaves and rejoins the level lookup.
+        // Off by default, prints only on a NULL <-> set transition, and cannot alter the assignment
+        // below. See LecithinTeleportRefusalDiagnostics.
+        if (fun.bm.lecithin.config.modules.CompatConfig.teleportRefusalDiagnostics) {
+            fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinTeleportRefusalDiagnostics.reportCallbackTransition(this, this.levelCallback, levelCallback);
+        }
+        // Lecithin end
         this.levelCallback = levelCallback;
     }
 
